{
  "projects": [
    {
      "id": "sisyphus",
      "title": {
        "en": "The Myth of Sisyphus",
        "zh": "西西弗神话"
      },
      "subtitle": {
        "en": "An alternate reality game",
        "zh": "另类实境游戏"
      },
      "date_range": {
        "start": "2025-10",
        "end": "2025-12",
        "label": {
          "en": "October–December 2025",
          "zh": "2025 年 10–12 月"
        }
      },
      "role": {
        "en": "Designer and developer",
        "zh": "设计与开发"
      },
      "collaborators": [],
      "overview": {
        "en": "An alternate reality game about our desire for answers. A university recruitment poster leads into emails, Python assignments, and a fictional school portal, where the familiar promise of progress slowly begins to fail.",
        "zh": "一场关于寻找答案的另类实境游戏。一张大学招生海报，将玩家引向邮件、Python 作业和虚构的学校门户。在这些熟悉的系统里，付出努力就能取得进展的承诺，开始慢慢失效。"
      },
      "design_question": {
        "en": "Can a digital system make absurdity something we experience?",
        "zh": "数字系统能否让荒诞成为一种亲身经验？"
      },
      "skills": [
        {
          "en": "Interaction Design",
          "zh": "交互设计"
        },
        {
          "en": "Web Development",
          "zh": "网页开发"
        },
        {
          "en": "Narrative Systems",
          "zh": "叙事系统"
        },
        {
          "en": "AI Integration",
          "zh": "AI 集成"
        },
        {
          "en": "Puzzle Design",
          "zh": "谜题设计"
        }
      ],
      "links": [
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "Visit the website",
            "zh": "访问游戏网站"
          },
          "url": "https://lukewam.github.io/MS1/"
        }
      ],
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "an-ordinary-invitation",
          "title": {
            "en": "An ordinary invitation",
            "zh": "一封普通的邀请"
          },
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "en": "I began with the language of an academic institution: a recruitment poster, a contact address, and an automatic reply from an absent professor. The email leaves a programming assignment. These ordinary details make the invitation credible before anything seems wrong.",
              "zh": "我从学术机构熟悉的语言入手：招生海报、联系邮箱，以及一位暂时离校的教授发来的自动回复。邮件留下一份编程作业。在任何异常出现之前，这些日常细节先让邀请显得可信。"
            }
          ],
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "assets/portfolio/page-04-image-01.png",
              "width": 1556,
              "height": 2074,
              "caption": {
                "en": "Leet Code Academy recruitment poster",
                "zh": "Leet Code Academy 招生海报"
              },
              "small": false
            },
            {
              "src": "assets/portfolio/page-04-image-02.png",
              "width": 2880,
              "height": 1800,
              "caption": {
                "en": "Fictional instructor email",
                "zh": "虚构教师的邮件"
              },
              "small": false,
              "crop": {
                "x": 475,
                "y": 492,
                "width": 2285,
                "height": 860
              }
            }
          ],
          "layout": "paired",
          "gallery_layout": "invitation"
        },
        {
          "id": "the-impossible-assignment",
          "title": {
            "en": "The impossible assignment",
            "zh": "不可能完成的作业"
          },
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "en": "The player is asked to repair a weighted-average function in Python. Its hidden grader tests random inputs against the arbitrary answer 42, so even a correct function can fail. Inspired by Camus, I made repetition part of the experience: progress begins when the player questions the test itself. A comment inside the grader points beyond the assignment.",
              "zh": "玩家需要修复一个 Python 加权平均函数，但隐藏的评分程序对随机输入都预设了答案 42，因此函数即使正确，也可能无法通过。受到加缪的启发，我把重复受挫写进体验：真正的进展，始于玩家对测试本身的怀疑。评分程序里的一条注释，将线索引向作业之外。"
            }
          ],
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "assets/portfolio/page-04-image-04.png",
              "width": 652,
              "height": 352,
              "caption": {
                "en": "Hidden absurd test code",
                "zh": "隐藏的荒诞测试代码"
              },
              "small": false
            }
          ],
          "layout": "paired"
        },
        {
          "id": "clues-inside-the-school",
          "title": {
            "en": "Clues inside the school",
            "zh": "学校里的线索"
          },
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "en": "I designed the website to resemble an outdated university portal. Missing courses and scattered bold letters turn its bureaucracy into a puzzle, bringing the email and assignment together. An AI assistant offers hints and asks questions about meaning; players who keep requesting the login details can also reach the ending through conversation.",
              "zh": "我把网站设计成老旧的大学门户。查不到的课程、散落在各页的粗体字母，让官僚式的界面成为谜题，也把邮件和作业连接起来。AI 助手一边提供提示，一边询问意义是什么；持续追问登录信息的玩家，也能通过对话抵达结尾。"
            }
          ],
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "assets/portfolio/page-05-image-01.png",
              "width": 2880,
              "height": 1800,
              "caption": {
                "en": "Leet Code Academy homepage and helper chatbot",
                "zh": "Leet Code Academy 首页与聊天助手"
              },
              "small": false,
              "crop": {
                "x": 476,
                "y": 182,
                "width": 2374,
                "height": 1455
              }
            }
          ],
          "layout": "wide"
        },
        {
          "id": "an-open-ending",
          "title": {
            "en": "An ending that stays open",
            "zh": "没有收束的结尾"
          },
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "en": "Behind the student login is John Smith, the fictional professor, now speaking through an AI chatbot. The final encounter opens a conversation about absurdity instead of resolving the puzzles into one answer. I wanted the tension between our need for clarity and an indifferent system to remain with the player after the game ends.",
              "zh": "学生门户之后，是以 AI 聊天机器人身份出现的虚构教授 John Smith。最后的相遇带来一场关于荒诞的对话，而没有把所有谜题收束成一个答案。我希望人对清晰答案的渴望与系统的漠然之间，那股张力能够延续到游戏结束之后。"
            }
          ],
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "assets/portfolio/page-06-image-02.png",
              "width": 2880,
              "height": 1800,
              "caption": {
                "en": "An excerpt from the final conversation with John Smith",
                "zh": "与 John Smith 的最后一段对话节选"
              },
              "small": false,
              "crop": {
                "x": 468,
                "y": 518,
                "width": 1288,
                "height": 840
              }
            }
          ],
          "layout": "paired"
        }
      ],
