        {
          "id": "keeping-the-menu-with-the-player",
          "title": {
            "en": "Keeping the menu with the player",
            "zh": "让菜单跟上玩家"
          },
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "en": "Testing exposed a practical issue: the menu needed to stay usable as the player moved. I attached it to the player model, adjusted its height dynamically, and hid it when unused. That kept the same tools available throughout the scene without leaving the menu permanently in view.",
              "zh": "测试中出现了一个实际问题：玩家移动后，菜单仍然需要便于使用。我将它绑定到玩家模型，动态调整高度，并在不用时隐藏。这样玩家在场景中移动时仍能调用同一组工具，菜单也不必一直挡在眼前。"
            }
          ],
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "assets/portfolio/page-12-image-01.png",
              "width": 1433,
              "height": 687,
              "caption": {
                "en": "Patient and medical equipment input flow",
                "zh": "伤者与医疗器材的输入流程"
              },
              "small": false
            }
          ],
          "layout": "paired"
        },
        {
          "id": "making-gestures-distinct",
          "title": {
            "en": "Making gestures distinct",
            "zh": "让手势容易区分"
          },
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "en": "We then mapped hand gestures to the existing controls with the Meta Interaction SDK. Some gestures were difficult for the headset to recognize, so I focused on simple, distinct movements. The work became a balance between what felt understandable to the player and what the tracking system could reliably distinguish.",
              "zh": "随后，我们通过 Meta Interaction SDK 将手势映射到已有操作。部分手势难以被头显识别，因此我重点设计简单、彼此差异清晰的动作。这个过程需要在玩家能否理解动作，以及追踪系统能否稳定区分动作之间，找到平衡。"
            }
          ],
          "images": [
