      "id": "autonomous-vehicle",
      "title": {
        "en": "Autonomous Vehicle",
        "zh": "自动驾驶小车"
      },
      "subtitle": {
        "en": "A small vehicle learning to read a track",
        "zh": "学习辨认赛道的自动驾驶小车"
      },
      "date_range": {
        "start": "2022-09",
        "end": "2022-12",
        "label": {
          "en": "September–December 2022",
          "zh": "2022 年 9–12 月"
        }
      },
      "role": {
        "en": "Hardware design and tracking software development lead",
        "zh": "硬件设计与循迹软件开发负责人"
      },
      "collaborators": ["Jerry Hung", "Michael Baluja"],
      "overview": {
        "en": "A camera-equipped vehicle built to follow a track and respond to signs. I constructed its hardware and developed the tracking software, moving from recorded driving demonstrations toward explicit color-based responses in OpenCV.",
        "zh": "一辆装有摄像头的小车，尝试沿赛道行驶并响应路标。我负责硬件搭建与循迹软件，先用驾驶示范训练模型，再通过 OpenCV 为颜色设置明确的响应规则。"
      },
      "tools": [
        "LightBurn",
        "Blender",
        "OpenCV",
        "NVIDIA hardware",
        "VESC motor controller"
      ],
      "links": [],
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "building-a-platform-to-test",
          "title": {
            "en": "Building a platform to test",
            "zh": "搭建可以测试的小车"
          },
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "en": "I assembled and wired the vehicle, designed its laser-cut acrylic chassis in LightBurn, and modeled protective housings in Blender for 3D printing. NVIDIA hardware, a camera, front depth sensing, and a central VESC motor controller formed the platform. A laptop connection provided live video and manual driving with arrow keys.",
              "zh": "我负责组装与接线，用 LightBurn 设计激光切割的亚克力底盘，并在 Blender 中建模、3D 打印保护外壳。车上装有 NVIDIA 硬件、摄像头、前置深度传感器与位于中央的 VESC 电机控制器。连接笔记本后，可以查看实时画面，并用方向键手动驾驶。"
            }
          ],
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "assets/portfolio/page-15-image-03.jpg",
              "width": 2420,
              "height": 1815,
              "caption": {
                "en": "Vehicle electronics and wiring assembly",
                "zh": "小车的电子部件与接线组装"
              },
              "small": false
            },
            {
              "src": "assets/portfolio/page-15-image-01.png",
              "width": 608,
              "height": 457,
              "caption": {
                "en": "Autonomous vehicle wiring diagram",
                "zh": "自动驾驶小车接线图"
              },
              "small": false
            }
          ],
          "layout": "paired"
        },
        {
          "id": "learning-from-thirty-laps",
          "title": {
            "en": "Learning from 30 laps",
            "zh": "从 30 圈驾驶中学习"
          },
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "en": "I collected 30 laps of manual driving under different lighting conditions, trained the model on a remote server, and deployed it to the vehicle. Track reflections disrupted its performance, so I repeated the training process. Lighting became a practical part of the problem, not just a background condition.",
              "zh": "我在不同光照下手动驾驶了 30 圈，用收集的数据在远程服务器上训练模型，再部署到小车上。赛道反光影响了表现，因此我多次重复训练。光照也从背景条件，变成了需要认真处理的实际问题。"
            }
          ],
          "images": [],
          "layout": "wide",
          "videos": [
            {
              "src": "assets/films/autonomous-vehicle-road-mat.mp4",
              "poster": "assets/films/autonomous-vehicle-road-mat-poster.jpg",
              "title": {
                "en": "Road-mat course",
                "zh": "道路垫场地"
              },
              "caption": {
                "en": "Onboard training footage from the marked track, with curves and strong window light.",
                "zh": "车载视角下的训练片段：标记道路上的弯道，以及窗边强光带来的明暗变化。"
              },
              "duration": 24,
              "width": 1920,
              "height": 1080
            },
            {
              "src": "assets/films/autonomous-vehicle-tape-course.mp4",
              "poster": "assets/films/autonomous-vehicle-tape-course-poster.jpg",
              "title": {
                "en": "Tape-line course",
                "zh": "胶带路线场地"
              },
              "caption": {
                "en": "A second training recording on tiled flooring, using blue tape to mark the route.",
                "zh": "另一段训练记录：在瓷砖地面上，以蓝色胶带标记行驶路线。"
              },
              "duration": 22,
              "width": 1920,
              "height": 1080
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "giving-colors-a-response",
          "title": {
            "en": "Giving colors a response",
            "zh": "为颜色设置响应"
          },
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "en": "We reworked the approach in OpenCV so responses could be programmed more directly. I wrote the color detection: white marked track edges, black the driving surface, light blue the boundary, and red a stop cue. This gave the team more control over behaviors such as stopping, parking, speeding up, and slowing down.",
              "zh": "团队随后用 OpenCV 调整方案，让车辆行为能够被更直接地编程。我负责编写颜色检测：白色表示赛道边缘，黑色表示行驶区域，浅蓝色表示边界，红色表示停止信号。这样，我们能更明确地设置停止、停车、加速与减速等响应。"
            }
          ],
          "images": [
            {
